id: pm-gh1678
title: "GH-1678: a scoped registerRenderer replacement bypasses --output-budget and its read_output receipt reports within_budget for the native payload, not the delivered bytes"
description: "GitHub issue #1678 (reported 2026-11-06 against 2026.11.5 from an agent-UX review). An extension command that declares read_output participates in host output controls, but when a scoped registerRenderer (SDK) replaces the TOON rendering, the host packs and measures the native structured payload and then writes the renderer's string without applying the caller's --output-budget. In the reporter's synthetic repro, --output-budget 400 --output-row-contract emits 10,780 B (about 2,695 tokens) while read_output reports estimated_tokens 179 and within_budget true. Native JSON (1,004 B) and native TOON (716 B) controls measure correctly. With --output-budget 1 the refusal exits 2 but is itself expanded through the renderer (10,574 B). Without the receipt flag the excess remains (10,073 B). Expected: the final-output ceiling applies to the string the selected renderer returns. If it cannot fit, the host returns the bounded native refusal with a nonzero exit, never routing a refusal back through the expanding renderer. A within_budget receipt must describe the delivered bytes. Unbounded artifact rendering stays available when explicitly requested. Duplicate check: searched renderer output budget, registerRenderer output, within_budget extension; GH-560 and GH-96 (closed) cover ignored or unscoped overrides, pm-gh1552 (closed) SDK compact-versus-pretty accounting, pm-gh1662 (open) native intent budgets. This item owns post-packing custom renderer output escaping the final-byte budget. Not yet reproduced locally; the repro block in the issue is executable."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ux,extensions,"gh:1678",output-budget,renderer,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-06T11:33:06.300Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T04:18:49.664Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-07T04:18:07.512Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-07T04:18:07.512Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The caller's --output-budget applies to the string a selected custom renderer returns, and output that cannot fit returns the bounded native output_budget_exceeded refusal with exit 2; A refusal is never routed back through an expanding custom renderer; read_output estimated_tokens and within_budget describe the delivered bytes of a custom rendering; Explicitly unbounded custom rendering stays available; A spec with a synthetic extension renderer asserts the bounded and unbounded behaviour in TOON and JSON, and a negative control that measures the native payload instead fails it"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Every read-output estimate, compaction step and omission decision now measures the delivered string: a scoped registerRenderer override, an output_format service string, the calendar markdown default or lean JSON (withDeliveredOutputRenderer in src/sdk/read-output-budget.ts; deliverContractedRead and deliverServiceRendering in src/core/output/output.ts). Output that cannot fit returns the bounded native output_budget_exceeded refusal with exit 2, and a refusal is never rendered through an override. A renderer's nested SDK contract calls measure their own representation. A custom rendering whose receipts understate it, which happens when the renderer depends on its own receipts, is re-measured and rendered natively, so no unmeasured byte is delivered. Undeclared commands and --output-budget unbounded keep unbounded custom rendering."
expected_result: "The caller's --output-budget applies to the bytes a custom renderer or output_format service delivers, receipts describe those bytes, and output that cannot fit is refused natively with exit 2"
actual_result: "Unit and integration specs (TOON and JSON renderer overrides, a service string, nested contract renderers, self-referential renderers) assert refusal with exit 2 at 400 and 1 tokens, fitting receipts equal to ceil(delivered bytes / 4), unbounded expansion kept, and negative controls that fail without each fix"
