comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T15:40:46.675Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check at creation (2026-11-06): pm search \"renderer output budget\" returned pm-5t33or (open, the declared-budget feature, now this item's parent), pm-prsvjh (closed, intent budget binding), pm-odw3j8 (closed, rendered relationship budgets), pm-gh1552 (closed, SDK compact JSON accounting), pm-t2t709 (closed, dependency budget measured on another representation) and pm-gd6vnn (open, observation contract). None covers a scoped registerRenderer replacement escaping the final-byte budget with a receipt measuring the native payload. The GitHub dedupe in the issue (#560, #96, #1552, #1662) reaches the same conclusion."
  "2026-11-07T01:36:59.220Z","harness:claude-code","Root cause: every read-output estimate, compaction step and omission decision measured formatBuiltInOutput's native rendering. formatEffectiveOutput then delivered a different string: a scoped registerRenderer override, or an output_format service result. A renderer that expands a 50-token payload to 10 KB therefore reported within_budget: true for bytes the caller never received, and the caller's --output-budget never applied to what was printed. Fix (branch fix/output-budget-delivered-bytes): withDeliveredOutputRenderer (internal, src/sdk/read-output-budget.ts) scopes estimateReadOutputTokens to the renderer the host will deliver, for the delivered encoding only, so receipts, compaction and omission measure the delivered string. The service path audits its string the same way. Output that cannot fit returns the native output_budget_exceeded refusal with exit 2. renderDelivered never routes a budget refusal through the override, so an expanding renderer cannot inflate it. Commands without a read_output declaration (for example pm-changelog's renderers) and --output-budget unbounded keep unbounded custom rendering. Evidence: tests/unit/core/output/delivered-output-budget.spec.ts covers TOON and JSON renderer overrides and the output_format service: refused natively with exit 2 at budgets 400 and 1, a fitting receipt equal to ceil(delivered bytes / 4), and unbounded expansion kept. Negative control: the native estimate is about 50 tokens against a 10 KB delivery. tests/integration/read-output/delivered-output-budget.integration.spec.ts drives a synthetic extension renderer through the real CLI from source. The defect's 179-token native estimate is the negative control there. pm test run passed."
  "2026-11-07T01:47:28.677Z","harness:claude-code","Codex batch review round 1 (P2), confirmed and fixed. When an output_format service string cannot fit, the bounded refusal is delivered natively (renderNative). But the delivered-renderer scope measured every value as the service string, including the refusal envelope itself, so the refusal's read_output.estimated_tokens described the service string instead. Reproduced: a 600-character service at --output-budget 150 delivered a 183-token JSON / 125-token TOON refusal whose receipt said 151. formatEffectiveOutput now measures a budget-omitted value natively, exactly as it is delivered. The regression in delivered-output-budget.spec.ts asserts receipt == ceil(delivered bytes / 4) for the service-triggered refusal in JSON and TOON. Negative control: with the old callback the 10 KB service reports 2,503 tokens for a 183-token refusal."
  "2026-11-07T02:03:13.638Z","harness:claude-code","Codex batch review round 2 (P2), confirmed and fixed. An extension renderer that computes its own SDK read-output contracts (attachReadOutputContracts on an embedded auxiliary read) inherited the outer delivered-renderer scope during measurement. At final delivery it ran with that scope restored, so the outer receipt measured different bytes than were delivered (503 tokens estimated for 446 delivered), and a budget just above the delivered size falsely refused with exit 2. estimateReadOutputTokens now invokes the delivered renderer with the measurement scope suspended (renderOutsideDeliveredScope in src/sdk/read-output-budget.ts), so nested calls measure their own representation in both phases. Regression: delivered-output-budget.spec.ts 'lets a renderer's own nested contract calls measure their own representation' asserts an exact receipt and no outer refusal at delivered+20. Negative control: with the old direct render call it fails with 503 vs 446."
  "2026-11-07T02:18:44.903Z","harness:claude-code","Codex batch review round 3: three P2s, one shared cause, all confirmed and fixed by one guard. A custom renderer whose output depends on its own receipts can leave a bounded estimate fixpoint at a value the final delivery exceeds: read_output reported 101 tokens for 1,001 delivered; the intent receipt claimed within_budget at 850 for 1,000 delivered; a read session charged 1,200 per call for 1,300 delivered, overrunning a 2,500 ceiling across two calls. Bounding the loops (round 2) prevents hangs but is no proof of fit. formatEffectiveOutput's contracted-read stage was extracted into deliverContractedRead (src/core/output/output.ts). It now checks the final custom rendering, before token accounting, which the receipts exclude by design, against read_output.estimated_tokens, context_intent.estimated_tokens and read_session.spent_this_call_tokens, and against the intent receipt's within_budget/token_budget claim. On any misstatement the read is re-contracted with native measurement and rendered natively, so no unmeasured byte is delivered, and an omission still exits 2. Without token accounting the check reuses the final rendering, so there is no extra render. Regressions in delivered-output-budget.spec.ts reproduce all three cases and assert truthful receipts, plus guards that a stable custom renderer is still delivered for intent reads, an unbounded intent read and token accounting. Negative control: with the check disabled the oscillating renderer's bytes are delivered (expected startsWith('x') to be false). docs/READ_OUTPUT_CONTRACTS.md states the rule."
  "2026-11-07T03:51:27.537Z","harness:claude-code","Final-tree refactor for the CodeFactor complexity ceiling (formatEffectiveOutput was 18 > 16). The built-in renderer factory (nativeRenderer) and the output_format service delivery (deliverServiceRendering) were extracted from formatEffectiveOutput, next to deliverContractedRead, with behavior unchanged. receiptsUnderstateDelivery dropped its intent fit-claim branch: settled intent receipts never claim a fit their estimate exceeds, so the estimate check covers it, and coverage showed the branch was unreachable. static-quality-gate.mts reports 0 complexity violations."
